WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.000
-A Democratic congresswoman
made a powerful speech

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.501
to her colleagues
to take action now

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:06.968
to solve
the cost-of-living crisis.

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:08.667
Also, we found out

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:11.334
that Donald Trump wanted
to bomb Mexico

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:13.334
and thought we could
pretend it wasn't us.

00:00:13.334 --> 00:00:16.334
Two stories, one look.
The classic two-hander.

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:18.667
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:20.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:25.667
The Republican Party remains
fully in thrall to Donald Trump,

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.634
even though he's
an aspiring authoritarian

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:28.634
and a crazy person.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:29.868
We've known that
for a long time,

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:32.200
and yet somehow we keep
learning more about

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.734
just how insane Trump is
on an almost daily basis.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.667
For example,
we found out this week

00:00:36.667 --> 00:00:39.834
that he asked his advisers
if China had a hurricane gun

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:42.934
they were shooting at us
to create severe weather events.

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:47.234
Now, I'm assuming Trump
was thinking of a giant weapon

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:49.901
that could create actual
Category 5 hurricanes.

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:52.801
But because his brain
only works in cartoons,

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:55.734
there's also a chance he thought
they had a tiny handheld gun

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:57.567
that shot out little rain clouds

00:00:57.567 --> 00:01:00.133
that would follow him around
wherever he went.

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:02.467
[As Trump] This is exactly
what they did the Daffy Duck.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.567
We love -- we love
Daffy Duck, don't we?

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:06.634
We love --
You know, I once met Daffy

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:09.834
on the dance floor at Studio 54
back in 1982.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:12.400
I met Daffy, and he said --
he came up to me

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.934
and he said something
I'll never forget.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.601
He said, "You...

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.434
You're despicable."
And...

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:19.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.767
And I said, "That's so true.
Daffy, that's so true."

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:23.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:25.901
[Normal voice] Yet somehow, that
was not the most insane thing

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.734
we learned recently,
because we also found out

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.868
from former Defense Secretary
Mark Esper

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.868
that Trump wanted to bomb Mexico

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.200
and thought we could
get away with it

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.667
because no one would know
it was us.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.667
-Former President Trump
reportedly wanted

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:40.400
to launch missiles into Mexico

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.868
to destroy
the drug labs and cartels.

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:46.167
The allegation comes from former
Defense Secretary Mark Esper.

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.467
In a new book obtained
by The New York Times,

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:51.167
Esper writes Trump asked him
at least twice

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:53.067
about the possibility
of the airstrikes

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:55.534
and said no one would know
it was the U.S.

00:01:55.534 --> 00:01:58.968
-The president pulls me aside
on at least a couple occasions

00:01:58.968 --> 00:02:02.334
and suggests that maybe
we have the U.S. military

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:04.300
shoot missiles into Mexico.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.334
-Shoot missiles into Mexico
for what?

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:08.701
-He would say to --
to go after the cartels.

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:10.534
I had to explain to him,
we can't do that.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:12.367
It would violate
international law.

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:15.868
-You politely pushed back
on the idea.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:19.567
Did President Trump really say
no one would know it was us?

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:21.534
-Yes. Yes.

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:22.868
He -- He said that,

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:24.734
and I just thought
it was fanciful, right?

00:02:24.734 --> 00:02:26.767
Because of course
it would be us.

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.968
I was reluctant to tell
the story

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:31.934
because I think -- I thought
people won't believe this.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:33.434
-No, I mean, we believe it.
Of course.

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:35.167
You know, we -- we believe it.

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:37.334
I mean, there's nothing you can
tell us about Donald Trump

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:40.467
that Donald Trump hasn't already
told us about Donald Trump.

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:43.133
The guy said with his own words
from his own mouth,

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:44.934
in public, on purpose,

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:47.200
that windmills cause cancer
and that we should inject

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.667
disinfectant into people's lungs
to cure coronavirus.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.901
If you told me Donald Trump
asked his advisers

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:53.801
in an Oval Office meeting
to form an alliance

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:55.868
with Godzilla
to steal the hurricane gun

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:58.400
and find all the fraudulent
ballots smuggled in from,

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.334
I don't know, Xanadu,
I'd be like,

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:02.167
"Sure, yeah, whatever.
I believe it."

00:03:02.167 --> 00:03:03.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.501
But still -- still,
I kind of can't get over

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.501
the fact that Trump
thought we could bomb Mexico

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:09.868
without anyone knowing
it was us.

00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:11.334
Imagine you're Mexico.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:12.801
The U.S. just had an election

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.834
where they chose
a visibly insane game show host

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:17.100
who said horrible things
about Mexicans,

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:20.400
and suddenly missiles
start raining down on you.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.767
Would you be mystified?

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.934
"Who's shooting these
Patriot missiles at us?

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:27.934
Did someone say something
that upset Costa Rica?"

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:30.767
So obviously it's critical

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:32.434
that we as a nation
do everything in our power

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:35.000
to prevent this obviously
unhinged demagogue

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.067
and his allies
in the Republican Party

00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:38.534
from regaining power.

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:41.467
And that, unfortunately,
is where the Democrats come in.

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:43.033
Oof!

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.767
It's like if you yelled,
"Avengers assemble!"

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:47.601
and only Hawkeye showed up.

00:03:47.601 --> 00:03:48.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:50.267
"And, uh, ehh...

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:54.767
FYI -- I did forget
my arrows, guys.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:58.100
It's gonna be the classic
Hawkeye punches."

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:01.000
If you've been paying any
attention at all to politics,

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.367
you know that Democrats
are in dire straits right now.

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:04.901
You don't need a poll
to tell you that.

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:06.234
All you have to do is watch

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:08.200
any Joe Biden press conference
with the sound off.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.767
He's always doing that thing
where he leans over the podium

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:13.734
like every question
is causing him physical pain.

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:15.067
He looks like --

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:17.200
looks like one
of Trump's advisers

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.834
after Trump asked about
the hurricane gun again.

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:21.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.234
"Yeah, they, uh...

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.834
They don't got
one of those, boss."

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:26.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:28.334
Anyway, things are bad
for Democrats.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.300
And that's not just me
saying that.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.534
Take congresswoman

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:33.200
and progressive rising star
Katie Porter,

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:36.100
who's perhaps best known
for using congressional hearings

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.767
to grill some of the nation's
most powerful figures,

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:41.434
from bankers to pharma CEOs
to oil executives,

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:42.934
using props like a whiteboard

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:45.968
where she calculates the cost of
living for a typical bank teller

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:49.033
or a big sign called
Financial Services Bingo.

00:04:49.033 --> 00:04:51.300
Everyone in Congress is so old,

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:54.100
she had to use bingo
to get their attention.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:57.934
"Quiet! Quiet!
She's calling out numbers!"

00:04:57.934 --> 00:05:00.367
Porter once even participated
in a hearing

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.701
with oil execs via Zoom
from her house

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:05.501
where she used bags of rice
in the trunk of her car

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:08.133
to help visualize
how much public land

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:10.200
oil companies could use
for drilling,

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.868
given that oil companies
were all opposed to a pause

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:17.000
on new federal drilling leases
on public lands.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.267
-How many acres of public land
are already leased

00:05:20.267 --> 00:05:23.767
by fossil fuel companies
and not even used yet?

00:05:23.767 --> 00:05:25.901
-I think you have
a fundamental misunderstanding

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:29.234
as to how this process works
and the time and resources --

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:31.534
-Reclaiming my time.
Reclaiming my time.

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:35.267
The answer is
13.9 million acres.

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:37.367
To visualize
how much land that is,

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:41.200
if each grain of rice
were one acre,

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:47.901
that would be
479 pounds of rice.

00:05:47.901 --> 00:05:50.968
The American Petroleum Institute
even opposed

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:52.801
pausing more leasing
on our lands,

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:54.400
they even sued to stop it,

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.467
because apparently this acreage
wasn't enough.

00:05:57.467 --> 00:05:58.901
Ms. Watkins,

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:02.234
do you support a pause on new
federal oil and gas leases?

00:06:02.234 --> 00:06:03.934
-No, I do not,
'cause I think it's important --

00:06:03.934 --> 00:06:06.801
-You already have
13.9 million acres.

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:09.501
This is equivalent to Maryland
and New Jersey combined.

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:11.267
How much more do you need?

00:06:11.267 --> 00:06:13.200
-First of all, I love
the dramatic reveal

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.634
when the automatic door
slowly opens.

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:18.133
I've never been so excited

00:06:18.133 --> 00:06:21.467
to see what's
in the trunk of a minivan.

00:06:21.467 --> 00:06:24.400
Usually when someone's opening
the trunk of a car like that,

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.334
it's a mobster
showing you a dead body.

00:06:27.334 --> 00:06:28.501
"Yeah, the minivan's great

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:29.834
'cause the back seats lift
right out.

00:06:29.834 --> 00:06:33.000
I can get, like,
five snitches in here.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.501
Used to have to take
a bunch of trips."

00:06:35.501 --> 00:06:38.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.667
It was such an effective
visual metaphor.

00:06:40.667 --> 00:06:42.133
If she had a music budget,

00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:45.734
she could have added the score
from "2001: A Space Odyssey."

00:06:45.734 --> 00:06:47.901
[ "Also Sprach Zarathustra"
plays ]

00:06:47.901 --> 00:06:56.767
♪♪

00:06:56.767 --> 00:06:58.968
I also love when
they cut back to her

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:00.901
and she's just standing there
stone-faced,

00:07:00.901 --> 00:07:02.567
pouring out a bag of rice

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:07.267
like it's some sort of
grain-based interrogation.

00:07:07.267 --> 00:07:09.934
The oil execs must have been
[bleep] their pants.

00:07:09.934 --> 00:07:12.300
"Tell me what I want to know,

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.300
or you can say goodbye

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.534
to your precious Rice-A-Roni."

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:20.000
"Please, God,
not the San Francisco treat!"

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.033
So, that --
that's Katie Porter.

00:07:22.033 --> 00:07:23.634
She's a rising star
in the Democratic Party,

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:24.801
and deservedly so.

00:07:24.801 --> 00:07:26.634
And now she is warning
her fellow Democrats

00:07:26.634 --> 00:07:29.334
about the peril
they face in the midterms

00:07:29.334 --> 00:07:32.934
unless they do something real
to improve people's lives.

00:07:32.934 --> 00:07:35.634
According to Politico,
Porter issued a wake-up call

00:07:35.634 --> 00:07:37.133
to her fellow
congressional Democrats

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:38.767
when she gave
an emotional speech

00:07:38.767 --> 00:07:42.267
about how inflation has been
hitting her family for months

00:07:42.267 --> 00:07:43.968
during a private
House Democratic Caucus

00:07:43.968 --> 00:07:45.300
meeting last week.

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:48.300
She said it seemed like
the first time the personal toll

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.934
of high consumer prices
had sunk in

00:07:50.934 --> 00:07:52.601
for some lawmakers in the room.

00:07:52.601 --> 00:07:54.901
Porter told Politico, "I had
a colleague mention to me,

00:07:54.901 --> 00:07:56.868
'We're not seeing it
in the polls.'"

00:07:56.868 --> 00:07:58.801
That's because
inflation is so bad,

00:07:58.801 --> 00:08:01.167
it's just screwing up
the poll results.

00:08:01.167 --> 00:08:02.834
[ Laughter ]

00:08:02.834 --> 00:08:04.534
And just to be clear,
I'm not saying inflation

00:08:04.534 --> 00:08:05.868
is somehow the Democrats' fault.

00:08:05.868 --> 00:08:07.267
They just happen to be
in charge now,

00:08:07.267 --> 00:08:09.033
so it's on them to do
something about it.

00:08:09.033 --> 00:08:11.400
But obviously, there are lots
of causes for rising costs,

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.767
including corporate greed,
supply chain problems

00:08:13.767 --> 00:08:16.601
caused by a pandemic
Trump let spiral out of control

00:08:16.601 --> 00:08:17.934
because he thought
it was a hoax,

00:08:17.934 --> 00:08:20.634
which is why it's so craven
and disingenuous

00:08:20.634 --> 00:08:22.367
when Republicans
shamelessly tweet

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:24.501
about how low gas prices
were under Trump.

00:08:24.501 --> 00:08:26.000
Like when Congressman
Jim Jordan tweeted...

00:08:29.701 --> 00:08:32.434
Yeah, man. I also remember
that no one was buying gas

00:08:32.434 --> 00:08:34.300
because we were all trapped
in our homes,

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.234
hiding from a deadly
respiratory disease

00:08:36.234 --> 00:08:39.567
your guy thought could be cured
by chugging a bottle of Windex.

00:08:39.567 --> 00:08:41.133
Fuel prices are based,

00:08:41.133 --> 00:08:42.934
among other things,
on supply and demand.

00:08:42.934 --> 00:08:44.567
And since no one
was traveling anywhere,

00:08:44.567 --> 00:08:47.167
meaning there were fewer cars on
the road and planes in the sky,

00:08:47.167 --> 00:08:48.601
gas was cheap as [bleep].

00:08:48.601 --> 00:08:51.868
It's the same reason
flat-screen TVs are cheap now,

00:08:51.868 --> 00:08:54.434
because you can watch "Avatar 2"
on your [bleep] phone.

00:08:54.434 --> 00:08:58.868
By the way, I'm told
you gotta see it that way.

00:08:58.868 --> 00:09:00.767
[ Laughter ]

00:09:00.767 --> 00:09:02.968
That's the way
to see "Avatar 2,"

00:09:02.968 --> 00:09:08.033
just with a phone
super close to your face.

00:09:08.033 --> 00:09:10.534
And don't put in EarPods.
Let everybody hear it.

00:09:10.534 --> 00:09:14.868
So, Republicans are obviously
lying when they pretend to care

00:09:14.868 --> 00:09:17.701
about the cost of living,
and they have no plan whatsoever

00:09:17.701 --> 00:09:19.200
to improve the lives
of working people.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.100
In fact, we found out today that
supposed pro-worker populist

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:25.033
Donald Trump colluded
with meat processors

00:09:25.033 --> 00:09:26.567
to keep their factories open

00:09:26.567 --> 00:09:28.601
even as COVID was ravaging
their workers.

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:30.767
So Republicans clearly don't
care about the working class.

00:09:30.767 --> 00:09:32.100
They're much more focused

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:34.067
on canceling Mickey Mouse
for being too woke.

00:09:34.067 --> 00:09:37.033
Democrats have given voters
so many reasons

00:09:37.033 --> 00:09:38.834
Republicans are insane,
they're probably like...

00:09:38.834 --> 00:09:40.601
-How much more do you need?

00:09:40.601 --> 00:09:42.601
-But still...

00:09:42.601 --> 00:09:45.133
Still, it is on Democrats

00:09:45.133 --> 00:09:47.334
to do something
to improve people's lives,

00:09:47.334 --> 00:09:50.200
like extend the massively
popular child tax credit

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:52.601
or invest directly
in green infrastructure,

00:09:52.601 --> 00:09:54.701
forgive student loan debt,
or expand healthcare.

00:09:54.701 --> 00:09:57.567
And look, I get it.
Joe Manchin is a giant ass-ache.

00:09:57.567 --> 00:09:59.734
The dude rakes in cash
from fossil fuels,

00:09:59.734 --> 00:10:02.701
drives a Maserati and lives
on a yacht called Almost Heaven,

00:10:02.701 --> 00:10:05.067
which sounds less like
the name of a yacht

00:10:05.067 --> 00:10:08.200
and more like the title
of an early-2000s rom-com

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:11.033
starring Ryan Reynolds
and Mandy Moore.

00:10:11.033 --> 00:10:12.400
Not my favorite movie,

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:15.367
but I watched it on an airplane
once and I cried so hard

00:10:15.367 --> 00:10:17.934
an air marshal had to tell me
to shut the [bleep] up.

00:10:17.934 --> 00:10:19.434
[ Laughter ]

00:10:19.434 --> 00:10:23.100
'Cause I guess feeling something
is against the law!

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.734
[ Laughter ]

00:10:24.734 --> 00:10:26.701
Manchin has been
stringing Democrats along

00:10:26.701 --> 00:10:29.000
for over a year now, so
Democrats just have to

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.167
call his bluff and say,

00:10:30.167 --> 00:10:32.667
"What will you accept?
We will pass it."

00:10:32.667 --> 00:10:34.868
Which is why it's frustrating
to read stuff like this

00:10:34.868 --> 00:10:36.534
in The Atlantic this week --

00:10:45.267 --> 00:10:47.934
What? Why?
Look, we all know Manchin sucks

00:10:47.934 --> 00:10:49.100
and he's gonna drag his heels,

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:50.934
but Chuck Schumer,
what are you waiting for?

00:10:50.934 --> 00:10:52.133
What's the problem here?

00:10:52.133 --> 00:10:55.801
Are your glasses too far
down your nose to read?

00:10:55.801 --> 00:10:57.367
Does he realize
glasses only work

00:10:57.367 --> 00:10:58.701
if they're in front
of your eyes?

00:10:58.701 --> 00:11:01.267
Would you -- would you like
another pair of glasses

00:11:01.267 --> 00:11:02.634
to help find your glasses?

00:11:02.634 --> 00:11:03.634
[ Laughter ]

00:11:03.634 --> 00:11:04.767
"Oh, look at that.

00:11:04.767 --> 00:11:07.100
They were way down
at the end of my nose.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.434
No wonder I couldn't govern."

00:11:08.434 --> 00:11:10.300
Just call --

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:12.968
call Manchin's bluff
and ask him what he wants.

00:11:12.968 --> 00:11:15.534
If Manchin's bull[bleep]
and his answer is actually

00:11:15.534 --> 00:11:18.801
that he's opposed to everything,
which is very possible,

00:11:18.801 --> 00:11:21.167
then at least we'll know
and we can move on.

00:11:21.167 --> 00:11:23.033
It's like when you're trying
to find something on TV

00:11:23.033 --> 00:11:25.334
to watch with your partner.
How about "Ozark"? Too dark.

00:11:25.334 --> 00:11:27.100
How about "Better Call Saul"?
Too slow?

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:29.400
At some point you just got
to hand over the remote and say,

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:30.934
"Okay, you pick something."

00:11:30.934 --> 00:11:33.767
And look, you'll probably end up
watching something called

00:11:33.767 --> 00:11:37.300
"The Teakettle Murders
on BritBox with the subtitles on

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.968
because everyone talks
like this --

00:11:38.968 --> 00:11:41.467
[ British accent ]

00:11:41.467 --> 00:11:43.167
[ Laughter ]

00:11:44.834 --> 00:11:47.434
But at least you're
watching something.

00:11:47.434 --> 00:11:49.767
And believe me, I know it sucks

00:11:49.767 --> 00:11:51.267
that this dude
gets to call the shots.

00:11:51.267 --> 00:11:53.667
I'd much rather live in a world
where the deciding vote

00:11:53.667 --> 00:11:55.300
was Katie Porter
instead of Joe Manchin.

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:57.067
But we do not live
in that world.

00:11:57.067 --> 00:11:59.167
We live in a world where
two obstructionist centrists

00:11:59.167 --> 00:12:01.834
are stopping the Democrats
from delivering on their agenda

00:12:01.834 --> 00:12:03.534
while an unhinged
Republican Party

00:12:03.534 --> 00:12:06.200
remains laser-focused
on dismantling democracy

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.434
and installing an authoritarian
demagogue in power.

00:12:08.434 --> 00:12:09.901
Republicans are so full of it,

00:12:09.901 --> 00:12:11.234
you'd think they just ate...

00:12:11.234 --> 00:12:16.367
-479 pounds of rice.

00:12:16.367 --> 00:12:17.534
[ Laughter ]

00:12:17.534 --> 00:12:19.534
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:19.534 --> 00:12:22.968
♪♪

00:12:22.968 --> 00:12:24.567
-God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:12:24.567 --> 00:12:26.801
over 2 million meals a year
to men, women, and children

00:12:26.801 --> 00:12:29.334
living with HIV/AIDS, cancer,
and other serious illnesses,

00:12:29.334 --> 00:12:31.133
and they need your help
now more than ever.

00:12:31.133 --> 00:12:33.234
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the donate button.

00:12:33.234 --> 00:12:35.634
Stay safe. Get vaccinated.
We love you.

